Aim:-
a. Write a program to implement numpy and pandas packages.

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Import Libraries
    . Import NumPy library as np
    . Import Pandas library as pd
3. NumPy Operations
    . Create an array using np.array() with elements [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
    . Store it in variable arr
    . Print the array
    . Calculate the sum of array elements using arr.sum()
    . Print the sum
5. Pandas Operations
    . Create a dictionary data with:
       . Key "name" and values ["a", "b", "c"]
       . Key "marks" and values [80, 90, 85]
    . Convert the dictionary into a DataFrame using pd.DataFrame(data)
    . Store it in variable df
    . Print the DataFrame
6. Stop

Code:-
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

#numpy

arr=np.array([1,2,3,4,5])
print("Aarray:",arr)
print("sum:",arr.sum())

#pandas

data={"name":["a","b","c"],"marks":[80,90,85]}
df=pd.DataFrame(data)
print("\n DataFrame: \n",df)

